<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# The wedding invitation's own layout. Deliberately shares nothing with
    layouts/application.html.erb — no nav, no site footer, no theme toggle, no
    terminal styling. The theme is fixed, so there is no light/dark cookie. %>
<%# No data-theme unless the guest has picked one: that's what lets daisyUI's
    prefersdark rule follow their device, with no flash and no JavaScript.
    tag.attributes drops the attribute entirely when the value is nil — an
    empty data-theme="" would still count as present and defeat the rule. %>
<html lang="en" <%= tag.attributes(data: { theme: wedding_theme(cookies[:wedding_theme]) }) %>>
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Our Wedding" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">

    <%# The guest list is private. Keep it out of search results entirely; the
        token in the URL is the only thing protecting it. %>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive">
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">

    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%# Turbo 8: replies to a broadcast refresh by morphing the DOM in place, so
        an RSVP landing from someone else's browser updates just the badge that
        changed and leaves the reader's scroll position alone. %>
    <%= turbo_refreshes_with method: :morph, scroll: :preserve %>
    <%# turbo_refreshes_with `provide`s its meta tags into :head rather than
        returning them, so this yield is what actually emits them. Without it
        the page silently falls back to a full replace on every broadcast. %>
    <%= yield :head %>

    <%# Every open invitation listens on the one stream the Guest model
        broadcasts to, which is what makes the guest list live. %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from :guest_list %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">

    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload", type: "module" %>
  </head>

  <body class="wedding-page min-h-dvh flex flex-col bg-base-100 text-base-content">
    <div class="fixed top-2 right-2 z-10">
      <%= theme_toggle_tag(light: "wedding",
                           dark: "wedding-dark",
                           cookie: "wedding_theme",
                           light_value: "light",
                           dark_value: "dark",
                           default_dark: false) %>
    </div>

    <%# Fixed to the viewport, not placed in the document: an RSVP redirect morphs
        the page with the scroll position preserved, so a banner at the top of
        <main> would land far above where the guest is actually looking. The
        wrapper renders unconditionally — daisyUI's .toast is position:fixed with
        no background, so an empty one is invisible and non-interactive. %>
    <div class="toast toast-end toast-bottom z-50">
      <% flash.each do |type, message| %>
        <%= flash_tag(message: message, type: type) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# The confetti surface for an accepted RSVP.
        canvas-confetti would otherwise append a canvas of its own to <body>, and the
        morph that follows the RSVP redirect deletes anything not in the new HTML — the
        burst would be wiped within a frame of appearing. This one is part of the
        document and marked permanent, so the morph leaves it alone. Same
        A *stable* id, unlike the flash toast's random uuid: Turbo pairs permanent
        elements across renders by id, and a fresh uuid each render means nothing
        matches, so the node is replaced and the in-flight animation dies with it.
        The toast gets away with a uuid because its replacement isn't in the new page
        at all; this canvas is, on every render. There's only ever one. %>
    <canvas id="wedding-confetti"
            data-wedding-confetti
            data-turbo-permanent
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 z-40 h-full w-full"></canvas>

    <main class="flex-1">
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <footer class="bg-base-200 border-t border-base-300 py-8 text-center text-sm text-base-content/70">
      <p class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
        <%= lucide_icon "heart", class: "h-4 w-4 text-primary" %>
        <span>We can't wait to celebrate with you.</span>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
